# Buttons

Do **not** create new button styles. Reuse the existing shared buttons exactly (hover, focus, disabled included).

## Primary fill (gradient)

- Component: `src/components/Button.astro`
- Surface class: `.btn` in `src/styles/global.css`
- Examples: Header “Let’s Talk”, Hero “Book a call”, Blogs “Read all”, Case Studies CTA, Contact submit

## Outline (white fill + brand gradient border)

- Component: `src/components/ButtonOutline.astro`
- Surface class: `.btn-outline` in `src/styles/global.css`
- Icon class inside slot: `.btn-outline__icon`
- Example: Locations “View Details”

## Allowed props / classes only

Pass label (slot), `href`, icon (slot), `type`, `size` (`default` | `nav` | `hero`), `loading`, `disabled`, `id`, `aria-label`, and **layout/width** utility classes (e.g. `!w-full`, `!w-[220px]`).

Do **not** override colors, gradient, radius, font, or hover effects.

## Extending

If something is missing (full-width, `type="submit"`, `id`), extend `Button` / `ButtonOutline` minimally with a prop or layout class — do not fork styles per section.

Dark service-card glass CTAs (`.service-card-btn`) are a separate card-chrome pattern, not a general site button. Do not use them as page CTAs.
